---
title: Cajun spiced fish tacos
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Mexican
tags: fish, fried
image: https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/uvuyxu1503067369.jpg
source: https://realfood.tesco.com/recipes/cajun-spiced-fish-tacos.html
---

On a large #plate{}, mix the @cajun seasoning{2%tbsp} and @cayenne pepper{1%tsp} with a little seasoning and use to coat the @white fish fillet{4} all over.

Heat the @vegetable oil{1%tsp} in a #frying pan{}, add in the @&white fish fillet{} and cook over a medium heat until golden. Reduce the heat and continue frying until the fish is cooked through, about ~{10%minutes}. Cook in batches if you don’t have enough room in the pan.

Meanwhile, prepare the dressing by combining the @sour cream{150%g}, @lemon{1} and @garlic{1%clove}(finely chopped) with a little seasoning.

Soften the @flour tortilla{8} in the #microwave{} for ~{10%seconds}. Pile high with the @avocado{1}(sliced), @little gem lettuce{2}(shredded) and @spring onion{4}(shredded), add a spoonful of @salsa{60%g}, top with large flakes of @&white fish fillet{} and drizzle over the dressing.
